lisa-design:
- SUPERSEDES the lookup-based JWT reuse (chart owner review on #30): no lookup and no render-time random/generated value anywhere. Credential precedence: existingSecret > externalSecret (ESO, refreshPolicy CreatedOnce) > explicit value > devSecrets.seed (dev only) > fail with one message listing every missing credential.
- devSecrets.seed derives sha256("ccf:<purpose>:<seed>")[:32] per purpose: deterministic across renders/upgrades/helm template, so the DB password never changes under an initialised database; empty by default so a plain install never uses it.
- ESO: Password generator + rewrite to the target key for passwords/Dex; the JWT key uses ESO template genPrivateKey (PKCS#1) because the SSHKey generator emits OpenSSH format the API cannot parse. Generated Secrets keep the old chart Secret names so templates reference one name.
- database.local / dex.clientSecret: existingSecret together with createSecret=true now fails loudly instead of silently picking one (old charts used the chart Secret in that case).
- Argo CD check (.github/workflows/argocd.yaml + ci/argocd/check.sh): render twice + no lookup, then a real Argo CD v3.5.4 on kind syncs both charts from the PR head SHA, waits Synced/Healthy, and requires Synced with no drifted resource after two hard refreshes. Lives here (where lookups are removed); it runs on stacked PRs too (no branch filter).

